# Plan Adherence

Before implementing any feature, creating any file, or adding any dependency, verify it
traces to the approved product plan.

## Feature Scope

All implementation work must map to an approved feature in `docs/feature-list.md`:

{{FEATURE_TABLE}}

| Feature | Scope |
|---------|-------|
| F1 | METAR → IWXXM conversion |
| F2 | IWXXM validation |
| F3 | Airport data services |
| F4 | IWXXM version handling |

Fill the feature table during stage 01-requirements. Until then, treat `[Scope Drift]`
as advisory when mapping exploratory work to planned features.

If work does not map to an approved feature, raise `[Scope Drift]` via AskQuestion:
- Cite the code or file being created
- Explain which feature it was intended for
- First option: "Map to feature FN — here's why..."
- Last option: "Let me explain / provide more context"

### Out of Scope (do not implement)

Document permanent exclusions in `docs/spec.md` §Non-Goals and `docs/feature-list.md`.
Do not implement capabilities listed there without an evolve cycle (16-evolve).

## Component Verification

New files must map to an approved component from `docs/spec.md` §Component Overview.

Fill the component table during 01-requirements / 04-tech-plan. Files outside approved
locations require justification. Raise `[Scope Drift]` if a new component is introduced
that is not in the spec.

## Dependency Verification

Before adding any new dependency, check `docs/dependency-inventory.md`. If the dependency
is not listed:
1. Raise `[Decision]` with a recommendation
2. On approval, back-add to `docs/dependency-inventory.md`
3. Record the decision in `workflow-state.yaml` §`decisions_log`
